# FIXED-BLOCKS-AUDIT: the words of a refusal name what they refuse in full.
# A held callable under a name of 300 bytes takes the arguments its header
# declares, two; one is refused where the call stands, with the callee's whole
# name in the words.  The name was copied into 160 bytes and the words into
# 200 before.
fn: make2 (int: n) fn: (int: x; int: y) int
    fn: f2 (int: x; int: y) int
        return: n + x * 10 + y
    return: f2
@:  make2(100)
int: r (1)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
